error[ffi_const_field]: `fixedbugs-2388-const-in-an-element.h` declares `Arm`'s member `k` as `const`, inside an element of one of `Arm`'s array members, so C still refuses to assign any `Arm` — and this line is that assignment
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2388-an-array-in-a-union-arm-is-told.hero:24:18
     |
  24 |     built: Arm = Arm(n: 1, rest: zero)  #~ ffi_const_field
     |                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: C11 counts a `const` member inside an array's element as it counts one at the top (C11 §6.3.2.1p1), though clang assigns it without a word: take one FROM the library through a pointer a function the group declares returns, rather than build it or receive it by value here

